        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">According to <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1965660#c8\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1965660#c8</a> <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/::-moz-focus-inner\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">::-moz-focus-inner</code></a> was effectively removed around FF89 (all this  issue does is final tidy up so that it is no longer in even parsed). The removal issue was <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1697053\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1697053</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">What I've done is marked it as removed in FF89 and indicated this is deprecated rather than experimental.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is that OK, or should we note the final version FF140 ?</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27011",
